{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require water quality results on all bills & monthly on company websites",
        "additional_details": "The public has a right to know what is in its drinking water. The USA requires annual water quality reports, and France provides information with water bills. The UK\u2019s Aarhus Convention obligations support public access to environmental information. PFAS, nitrates, lead, pesticides and other contaminants can threaten health and the environment. Monthly disclosure of test results, limits and failures would give customers the transparency needed to judge the quality of water they pay for.",
        "background": "Require water companies to publish drinking-water quality results on every customer bill and update results on their websites at least monthly, listing contaminants detected, their concentrations, legal limits or guidelines, and all breaches, including dates, readings and frequency of failures.",
